# Sample environment for mecab-furigana-rs.
# Copy to `.env` and uncomment the variables you need.  Real environment
# variables always win over `.env`; this file only fills in unset ones.

# ── MECAB_DICT_DIR ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Path to a MeCab UTF-8 system dictionary directory (the one containing
# `sys.dic`).  Only needed if your dictionary is not in a standard Linux
# path that the crate already probes.
#
# Examples by platform:
#   macOS / Homebrew (Intel):  /usr/local/lib/mecab/dic/ipadic
#   macOS / Homebrew (Apple):  /opt/homebrew/lib/mecab/dic/ipadic
#   Manual / source install:   /usr/local/lib/mecab/dic/naist-jdic
#   Windows (default install): C:\Program Files\MeCab\dic\ipadic
#
#MECAB_DICT_DIR=/opt/homebrew/lib/mecab/dic/ipadic

# ── MECAB_USER_DICT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional compiled user dictionary file(s), layered on top of the system
# dict to add missing words/kanji readings.  Accepts a single path or a
# comma-separated list (matches MeCab's own `-u a.dic,b.dic` syntax).
#
# Build a `.dic` from a CSV with `mecab-dict-index`:
#   mecab-dict-index -d "$MECAB_DICT_DIR" -u mydict.dic \
#                    -f UTF-8 -t UTF-8 mydict.csv
#
# CSV row format (must match the system dict's column count, typically 13):
#   surface,left-id,right-id,cost,POS,POS1,POS2,POS3,conj-form,conj-type,base,reading-kata,pron-kata
# Example (use left-id/right-id 0 and a small cost to let MeCab assign them):
#   表面,0,0,5000,名詞,固有名詞,*,*,*,*,表面,ヒョウメン,ヒョウメン
#
#MECAB_USER_DICT=./mydict.dic
#MECAB_USER_DICT=./names.dic,./neologisms.dic
